    "body": "<!--\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\n  for our PR guidelines.\n-->\n\n## Problem\nIn a terminal buffer in Normal mode (\"nt\"), the 'messagesopt' pager key\ndoesn't enter the pager after a command shows a collapsed message. The\nmode check matches \"i\" or \"t\" anywhere in the mode string, so \"nt\" is\ntreated as Terminal mode.\n\n## Solution\nMatch only the first character of the mode string, like the Visual mode\ncheck in the same file.\n",
